+### 2026-08-14 Structural Performance Review
+
+- Current viewer startup decodes the complete HDR pixel payload before the
+  importer can determine that its persisted `.zcube` and `.zribl` are current.
+  A cache hit therefore still pays the pixel decode and exposure scan.
+- cmft splits PMREM by mip and face, while cmftStudio runs its filter as a
+  background job and publishes a completed result before recreating GPU
+  buffers. Zircon retains its headless, atomic asset-derived producer instead
+  of importing a UI-thread model into the asset pipeline.
+- The next structural optimization is a header-only canonical request probe
+  followed by validated complete-bundle restore. A missing exposure sidecar
+  returns to the established pixel-decode-and-stage path; it does not weaken
+  cache identity, PMREM/IEM recipe semantics, or corrupt-artifact recovery.
+
+### 2026-08-14 Viewer Warm-Cache Preparation
+
+- Prepared, not accepted: the importer derives its canonical request from HDRI
+  header dimensions and source bytes before pixel decoding, then restores only
+  a complete current `.zcube` plus asset-derived `.zribl` environment.
+- The viewer retains cold-path exposure exactly through a versioned sidecar
+  named beside the source `.zcube`; a missing or malformed sidecar forces the
+  established decode-and-stage fallback. Pixel decode is never skipped unless
+  the restored environment and exposure both validate.
+- M8 remains `in_progress`. This forward work has static patch-application and
+  whitespace evidence only; coordinator integration, Rust/WGPU compilation,
+  target-machine timings, screenshot verification, and RenderDoc replay remain
+  pending.
